From: Daniel Ramos (Capitain Jack) <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 12:00:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] systemtray: release the mouse areas around the applet when its context menu opens

SystemTray::showPlasmoidMenu() releases the press that opened the menu (the popup takes the release, QTBUG-59044) through QQuickWindow::mouseGrabberItem().
Outside an event delivery that function answers null, with the warning "mouse grabber ambiguous: no event is currently being delivered", as soon as
several pointing devices have been in use (a touchpad beside a mouse, a compositor's virtual pointer). Then nothing is released: the tray item's MouseArea
stays pressed after the menu closes, and the next right click on the item is spent clearing that, so an applet's menu opened on every second right click only
(measured in a Plasma 6.7.4 login: 5 menus of 10 right clicks with the stock plugin, 10 of 10 with this change; the stock Clipboard and Disks & Devices
items alternate the same way).
The mouse areas of the applet's ancestors are released instead; releasing an area that holds no grab does nothing.
Origin: ours; master of plasma-workspace has the same code on 2026-11-18, not reported upstream (one report at a time).
Assisted-by: claude-sonnet-5-5
---
--- a/applets/systemtray/systemtray.cpp
+++ b/applets/systemtray/systemtray.cpp
@@ -329,9 +329,20 @@
     // this causes the next click to go missing
 
     // by releasing manually we avoid that situation
+    //
+    // QQuickWindow::mouseGrabberItem() used to find the item holding the press. Outside an event delivery it answers null, with the warning
+    // "mouse grabber ambiguous: no event is currently being delivered", as soon as more than one pointing device has been in use (a touchpad beside a mouse,
+    // a compositor's virtual pointer), so the workaround did nothing: the tray item's MouseArea stayed pressed, and the next right click on the item was
+    // spent clearing it (the menu opened on every second right click only). The mouse areas around the applet are released instead.
     auto ungrabMouseHack = [appletInterface]() {
-        if (appletInterface->window() && appletInterface->window()->mouseGrabberItem()) {
-            appletInterface->window()->mouseGrabberItem()->ungrabMouse();
+        QQuickItem *item = appletInterface;
+        for (int depth = 0; item && depth < 12; item = item->parentItem(), ++depth) {
+            const auto children = item->childItems();
+            for (QQuickItem *child : children) {
+                if (child->inherits("QQuickMouseArea")) {
+                    child->ungrabMouse();
+                }
+            }
         }
     };
 
